# fem-em-solver scheduled automation — see docs/automation/ in the repo.
#
# WIND-DOWN SCHEDULE (operator directive 2026-09-13): the token budget is cut
# by at least 4x and the project continues slowly rather than stopping.
#   - One Fable daily review (45 min cap) at 03:00, followed by four Opus
#     implementer runs (65 min hard kill) at 04:30 / 06:00 / 07:30 / 09:00 —
#     one overnight block per active day, inside the quiet hours on the
#     shared box. Under the take-next rule (implementer-run.md step 2) four
#     slots landed eight items on 2026-09-13; the §9 restock floor of 240
#     slot-minutes was defined for exactly this four-slot interval.
#   - Tuesday and Thursday are OFF: no reviews, no implementer runs.
#     Active days are Sun Mon Wed Fri Sat = 0,1,3,5,6. Every entry in the
#     block sits on one calendar day, so the day-of-week field is exact.
#   - One weekly planning review (Fable, 60 min cap), Saturday 21:00 —
#     moved off Sunday 02:15 because on 09-06 and 09-13 that session
#     exhausted the account's 5-hour allowance in ~20 min and took the 03:00
#     review and the 04:30 / 06:00 slots with it. Saturday 21:00 is its own
#     window (it ends by 02:00 Sunday), Saturday's slots are long done, and
#     the Saturday XXL result (02:00–10:00) is in the ledger to be read.
#     The Wednesday weekly is dropped; what the plan calls "the 09-16
#     weekly" is the 09-19 one.
#   - XL / XXL windows and housekeeping are UNCHANGED: cron scripts with no
#     Claude session, zero tokens — the cheapest compute the project has.
# Sessions never overlap; all Claude runs share one flock. Per-command compute
# stays under the repo's tier ceilings. Previous 16-slot grid: git history.
0 3 * * 0,1,3,5,6 /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/daily-review.sh
30 4 * * 0,1,3,5,6 /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/implementer-run.sh
0 6 * * 0,1,3,5,6 /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/implementer-run.sh
