0 9 * * 0,1,3,5,6 /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/implementer-run.sh
0 21 * * 6 /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/weekly-review.sh
# Sunday 01:45: mechanical log-retention sweep (no Claude session; ~1 min).
# See docs/testing/retention-policy.md §4.
45 1 * * 0 /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/housekeeping.sh
# 02:00 Sun-Fri: the XL window (4 h, 512 GiB — 2026-09-13; was 2 h), if one is queued in
# docs/testing/xl-queue.env (operator directive 2026-09-09). No Claude
# session — a cron script has neither the 660 s foreground cap nor the 65-min
# slot kill. 02:00 because the box is shared with work this sandbox cannot
# see. Own lock, not the automation flock. Budget six per trailing 7 days (2026-09-13),
# enforced by the guard against xl-ledger.md; fires nightly and does nothing
# once the budget is spent or the queue is empty. Worst case ends 06:00, so a
# full window overlaps the 04:30 implementer slot (and the 06:00 one at its
# kill): 16 XL ranks plus a 2-8 rank slot job on the 36-core box, accepted by
# the operator 2026-09-13 as the price of the longer window; the XL job holds
# its own lock, not the automation flock, so neither waits for the other.
0 2 * * 0-5 /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/xl-run.sh xl
# 02:00 Saturday: the XXL window (8 h, 754 GiB, one per week), from
# docs/testing/xxl-queue.env. Its own day so the two tiers never both
# start at 02:00; 8 h from 02:00 ends at 10:00 and overlaps the 04:30-09:00
# slots (2-8 rank jobs on a 36-core box — the one deliberately oversubscribed
# window). Operator directive 2026-09-10.
0 2 * * 6 /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/xl-run.sh xxl
